The test setup in `tests/drivers/i2c/i2c_emul/boards/native_sim.overlay` configures `i2c0` to forward requests to two other I2C buses, `i2c1` and `i2c2`. For the buffered mode test, `i2c1` is configured with `target-buffered-mode`, but `i2c2` is not. This mixed configuration of buffered and non-buffered (PIO) forwarded buses likely exposes a bug in the I2C emulator controller driver.

The fix is to make the configuration consistent by enabling `target-buffered-mode` for `i2c2` as well. This ensures that when testing buffered mode, all forwarded buses operate in the same mode, avoiding the buggy code path in the driver.

